@startuml

@startuml

title A secret is written sealed, and resolved sealed

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "a person\n(an HTTP client)" as person
participant "ores.http\n(the gateway)" as gateway
participant "ores.vault" as vault
database "ores_vault_* rows" as dbv
participant "systemd\n(the consumer's unit)" as systemd
participant "a consumer\n(for example ores.iam)" as consumer

== the write ==

person -> gateway : the provider's client secret\n(HTTPS, the gateway's own route)
gateway -> gateway : seal to the vault's transport public key\n(vault.v1.ops.public_key; not a secret)
gateway -> vault : vault.v1.ops.write\n(tenant, name, owner, sealed payload)
vault -> vault : the caller holds vault::secrets:write
vault -> vault : open with the vault's transport\nprivate key (a system credential)
vault -> vault : seal under the key encryption key\n(AAD: tenant | name | owner | version)
vault -> dbv : one row: nonce, tag, ciphertext, version
vault --> gateway : accepted (name, version)\nno value in the reply

== the resolve, at a consumer's start ==

systemd -> systemd : LoadCredential: the NATS\ncredential, and the consumer's\ntransport private key
systemd -> consumer : CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY
consumer -> consumer : connect to NATS over mTLS
consumer -> vault : vault.v1.ops.resolve\n(Authorization: the service's token; tenant, name)
vault -> vault : the token's subject holds\nvault::secrets:resolve
vault -> dbv : read the row for (tenant, name)
vault -> vault : open under the key version\n(AAD: tenant | name | owner | version)
vault -> vault : look up the caller's public key\nby the token's subject,\nnever from the request
vault -> vault : seal to that public key\n(AAD: subject | name | version)
vault --> consumer : ciphertext
consumer -> consumer : open with its own private key\n(in memory only)
consumer -> consumer : use it: open the pool,\npresent it, sign a token

note over vault, consumer
  The bus carries ciphertext in both
  directions. The broker keeps the
  metadata and the ciphertext; it
  keeps no value.
end note

@enduml
